Enable the compute DSP used by the OEM Goodix algorithm firmware.

The SM8450 base node already describes the CDSP PAS interrupts, power domains,
GLINK/FastRPC channel and 32 MiB reservation. Select the installed Unicorn signed
image, rather than leaving the node disabled and losing /dev/fastrpc-cdsp.

The OEM cape DT also supplies NSP -> DDR bandwidth for boot. qcom_q6v5_prepare
already votes the first interconnect until handover (and unwinds on failure),
but without this property that vote is a no-op. Retain the same boot path.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-dsp.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-dsp.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-dsp.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-dsp.dtsi
@@ -15,3 +15,10 @@
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8475/xiaomi/unicorn/slpi.mdt";
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&remoteproc_cdsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8475/xiaomi/unicorn/cdsp.mdt";
+	interconnects = <&nsp_noc MASTER_CDSP_PROC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
+			 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
